+    /// The terminal (`Finalized`, `Detached` or `Dropped`) was handed to the
+    /// transport behind every record before it. Over the mux: the batch
+    /// carrying it was admitted. On the same worker: it is in the anchor's
+    /// channel. On a per-stream transport: it is in the egress channel.
+    Sent,
+    /// The stream's slot or channel went away with output not handed on:
+    /// the consumer cancelled or dropped its anchor, the peer epoch died, or
+    /// this node shut down.
+    Discarded,
+}
+
+/// Resolves once velo on this node holds none of the stream's output.
